# React Learning Notes

- When implementing a React 19 API or pattern, explain what it does and why it is being used.
- Compare every newly introduced React 19 concept with its React 18.2 equivalent or workaround.
- Include the comparison in the implementation summary so the developer can learn from the change.
- Add a concise file-level learning comment when a file introduces a React 19 concept.
- Place learning comments only at the top or bottom of the file, never between imports, logic, or JSX.
- In the comment, name the React 19 feature and briefly state how React 18.2 handled the same need.
- Keep comments current when the related implementation changes.
- Do not add comments that merely narrate obvious code.
- Keep detailed explanations in the implementation summary rather than turning source files into tutorials.
